<BlogPost slug="how-to-stop-anxiety-after-drinking-alcohol" toc={toc}>
  <p>Drinking and anxiety have a cyclical relationship. Many people consume alcohol in an attempt to mask anxiety, but the next day, feel more anxious because of drinking. There's even a colloquial term for it: hangxiety (hangover + anxiety).</p>
  <p>Alcohol affects your brain chemistry, and after just one or two drinks, you're more likely to feel anxious afterward. People who have existing mental health conditions are more likely to be impacted and more severely.</p>
  <p>The best way to avoid stress, low mood, or worrying after drinking is to not drink alcohol. It also helps to understand how alcohol impacts your internal systems, and what factors make alcohol-induced anxiety more intense.</p>

